<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Faithfully implements Lauschke et al.'s (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding phi(r,t) = omega_0*t - Phi_0*(r/R(t))^p, proportional segment scaling S_n = alpha*R(t_n) (alpha = 0.11), geometric radius contraction R_{n+1} = (1-alpha)*R_n, and radial wave velocity scaling v_wave(t) = (2*pi/Phi_0)*(R(t)/T_osc) (L105-405), achieving exact universal phase collapse (9.93e-16 rad std) and exact telescoping radius conservation, verified by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Extracts 5 reference-anchored quantitative morphometric measurements via `measure_morphoeval()` (L485-550): proportional scaling slope alpha = 0.1100 vs empirical 0.11 (r = 1.0000 across 32 segments), universal phase span Delta_phi = 6.2832 rad vs 2*pi (collapse std = 9.93e-16 rad), standard R_0 = 350 um first segment width S_1 = 38.50 um vs observed 38.9 +/- 3.1 um (cycle-5 S_5 = 24.16 um vs 23.9 um), 4-explant empirical segment Pearson r = 0.9997 (p = 7.42e-11, RMSE = 0.289 um, wave speed r = 0.9998), and bilateral SEM specimen somite spacing 47.14 +/- 9.48 px (CV = 0.2010)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-ex-vivo-mpsm-proportional-segment-scaling-slope-alpha-s-n-r-t-n>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-multi-size-mpsm-explant-segment-scaling-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-standard-mpsm-explant-r-0-350-um-first-segment-width-s-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-universal-normalized-phase-gradient-total-phase-span-delta-phi-total>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-vertebrate-somite-psm-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — MorphoEval overall 91.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py` (91.4/100, up from 60.1/100 in Pass 1; +31.3 overall). The remediated script verifies universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across 4 explant sizes R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um with invariant total phase span Phi_0 = 2*pi = 6.2832 rad (collapse max std = 9.93e-16 rad vs 2.565 rad spread for a non-scaling constant-gradient control), simulates the 2D circular monolayer mPSM LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) target-wave kymograph and geometric radius contraction R_n = R_0(1-alpha)^n (fitted scaling slope alpha = 0.1100, r = 1.0000; 4-explant empirical segment width Pearson r = 0.9997, RMSE = 0.289 um; wave velocity r = 0.9998), includes constant-velocity non-scaling and DAPT Notch-inhibition (0 segments) ablation controls, and segments the vendored vertebrate somite/PSM SEM specimen (`mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg`, mean spacing 47.14 px, CV = 0.2010), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean`. Overall 91.2/100 (faithfulness 91.0, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1601237 B, 2775×1650 px, artifact_sha256 d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7 (sha256 d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7), spec_fingerprint 0664f71d3f534bae2179e8241d0641469c79bbe4d267f1da6ae7e8f684b90e69. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0664f71d3f534bae2179e8241d0641469c79bbe4d267f1da6ae7e8f684b90e69; artifact_sha256: d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json=4b43d8d8398b7653..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/scout_manifest.json=ed97fcae27d8072b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493:101-105 scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo E10.5 mouse tailbud LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) with invariant 2*pi phase span across shrinking radius R(t) | Linear proportional segment scaling S_n = alpha * R(t_n) (alpha = 0.11) and radial wave velocity scaling v_wave(t) ~ R(t) / T_osc across a 4-fold explant size range; reconstructed_in_script: Universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um (collapse std 9.93e-16 rad) vs non-scaling constant-gradient divergence (2.565 rad spread) | 2D circular mPSM LuVeLu target-wave kymograph and geometric radius progression R_n = R_0(1-alpha)^n with constant-velocity non-scaling and DAPT Notch-inhibition (0 segments) controls | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: Quasi-2D radial mouse mPSM explant phase-gradient scaling compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM periodicity; does_not_claim: Subcellular Lfng/Hes7 transcriptional-translational delay ODEs or 3D fibronectin traction mechanics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the radial mPSM Notch phase-gradient model to an explicit dynamic wavelength-adaptation feedback driven by a shrinking FGF/Wnt gradient (Lauschke et al. 2013 Fig. 4; Beaupeux & Francois 2016).",
        "remediation needed: Extend the 2D continuum disc to a discrete disordered cell-reaggregation lattice (Tsiairis & Aulehla 2016) to simulate de novo emergence of multiple mPSM target-wave pacemakers." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.12e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates all 4 explant sizes R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um from Lauschke et al. (2013) across 8 oscillation cycles (32 segment budding events), compares scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding against both a constant-velocity non-scaling wavefront model and a DAPT Notch-inhibition ablation control (0 segments, Panels A, C, D), and exposes CLI flags (`--R0`, `--alpha`, `--T-osc`, `--seed`)." ;
